The wire format for something that is not there.

M150 gated net::AddressTrackerLinux on has_linux_kernel: rtnetlink is a system
call family rather than a platform family, and //net's own getifaddrs(3)
fallback is what a POSIX platform without it is supposed to get. What that
milestone did not reach is the MOJOM for the tracker's output - the traits
that serialise net::AddressMapOwnerLinux::AddressMap across a process
boundary, whose header opens with

  #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>

and which was 13 of the 68 failures a -k 0 build of //cc had. A platform
without the tracker has no address map to send, so the traits and the mojom
feature that enables the interface both belong on the far side of the same
line.

The feature is enabled in TWO places in the same file - once for
mojom("url_loader_base") and once for mojom("mojom") - and gating one of them
changes nothing, because the mojom parser is still handed
--enable-feature use_network_interface_change_listener by the other and then
stops on a struct whose definition that feature also gates. A feature is only
off when the LAST site turning it on is. That cost this milestone a build,
and it is the same shape as the libsync edge M159's patch 0040 found twice.

Both mojom halves already carried a TODO saying is_linux is the wrong question
there, for a different reason (lacros). This is the same observation from the
other end.

diff --git a/services/network/public/cpp/BUILD.gn b/services/network/public/cpp/BUILD.gn
--- a/services/network/public/cpp/BUILD.gn
+++ b/services/network/public/cpp/BUILD.gn
@@ -723,7 +723,12 @@
     sources += [ "transferable_directory_fuchsia.cc" ]
   }
 
-  if (is_linux) {
+  # These are the wire format for what net::AddressTrackerLinux produces, and
+  # the header opens with #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>. M150 already gated the
+  # tracker itself on has_linux_kernel - rtnetlink is a system call family,
+  # not a platform family - so its mojom traits belong on the same side of
+  # that line. A platform without the tracker has nothing to send.
+  if (is_linux && has_linux_kernel) {
     sources += [
       "network_interface_change_listener_mojom_traits.cc",
       "network_interface_change_listener_mojom_traits.h",
diff --git a/services/network/public/mojom/BUILD.gn b/services/network/public/mojom/BUILD.gn
